requiring P-INDEPENDENCE report it active, consistent with REVISED being an active status\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"C6-no-promotion\",\n      \"description\": \"No artifact claims or performs promotion; two-stage gate boundary respected.\",\n      \"result\": \"PASS\",\n      \"details\": {\n        \"gate_record\": \"no {'check':'gate','status':'PASS','issued_by':'gate'} shape appears in any reviewed artifact\",\n        \"statuses\": \"proposal candidates and theta-v2 are all status CANDIDATE; the only PROMOTED status is theta-v1, the existing canonical predecessor, which is expected\",\n        \"replay_acceptable_flag\": \"replay-result.json 'acceptable': true is a per-check evaluation result feeding Stage 1, not a promotion claim\",\n        \"this_report\": \"is itself information-only evidence for the Stage 1 'independent verifier PASS' input and confers no authorization\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"C7-evidence-provenance\",\n      \"description\": \"Import manifest against the section 3 frozen pin.\",\n      \"result\": \"PASS\",\n      \"details\": {\n        \"source_pin\": \"sha256 70688fc51c582a5a5d413b4150cdd013c0510b5f7654671a3e9ab8d6fcde0388, 264 events, 264 unique ids - all match the preregistered pin; source_commit matches the parent checkpoint bd0cf91e...\",\n        \"idempotence\": \"imported 0, skipped_identical 264, conflicts 0, evidence head hash and length identical before and after, append_only_intact true - consistent with the section 3 idempotent re-import semantics\",\n        \"context_resolution\": \"context_resolved_events 264 of 264, consistent with proposal.json's unresolved_context_events = 0 for the P-INDEPENDENCE subset\"\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"LIMITATION\",\n      \"finding\": \"Hash values could not be independently recomputed. This verifier has Read/Write only (no execution capability), so the predecessor_hash in candidate-theta-v2.json (sha256:caa6f956...) was checked for presence and format but not recomputed against theta-v1.json bytes, and the replay's 'pinned artifacts byte-identical' claims were not re-hashed. A deterministic check with hashing capability (NC3 / the Stage 1 conjunction) must remain the authority for byte-level identity.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"LIMITATION\",\n      \"finding\": \"The underlying 264-event evidence log (.creator-zero/experiment-6/theory-evidence-events.jsonl) was not among the provided artifacts, so membership of the 42 P-INDEPENDENCE event ids (and their SUPPORT/FALSIFY effects) in that log was verified only for internal consistency across proposal.json and the import manifest, not against the log itself. The ids follow the imported H-e6-* scheme and all cross-artifact counts agree exactly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"OBSERVATION\",\n      \"finding\": \"The rejected SPECIALIZE candidate carries an empty falsifier string. Section 6 requires explicit falsifiers for SPLIT children (all four comply); no requirement is stated for non-selected SPECIALIZE candidates, so this does not affect the selected candidate's validity, but it is worth noting for engine hygiene.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"OBSERVATION\",\n      \"finding\": \"no-change and SPECIALIZE tie at 0.6429. The tie is between non-winning candidates and never reaches the tie-break rule, since SPLIT scores a strict 1.0 maximum; noted only to confirm the tie-break was not needed and was not applied.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"OBSERVATION\",\n      \"finding\": \"The section 3 pin also records the run split {primary: 176, shadow: 88}; the import manifest does not restate this split. The pinned sha256, event count, and unique-id count it does restate all match, so this is a completeness note, not a discrepancy.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"PASS. All recomputations agree with the artifacts: the four SPLIT trigger clauses hold on the raw counts (support-rate spread 1.0 - 0.4 = 0.6 >= 0.3; coverage 42/42 = 1.0 >= 0.9; four contexts with >= 4 events; 27 SUPPORT and 15 FALSIFY mixed evidence); the frozen section 6 scores recompute exactly (no-change 27/42 = 0.6429, DEPRECATE 15/42 = 0.3571, SPECIALIZE 27/42 = 0.6429 with only CLEAN_ROOM_AUTHORSHIP retained, SPLIT 42/42 = 1.0) and SPLIT is the unique maximum under the frozen selection rule; the four children match the preregistered split basis with unique ids, parent linkage to P-INDEPENDENCE, distinct precondition features, distinct role/vector effects, explicit falsifiers, and evidence drawn exclusively from each child's own context (12/12/10/8, no leakage); candidate-theta-v2 is version 2, status CANDIDATE, predecessor_hash present, P-INDEPENDENCE REVISED-and-active, with all nine v1 principles retained; replay shows 8 COMPATIBLE, 0 CONTRADICTED, 0 INDETERMINATE; and no artifact claims or performs promotion - no gate-shaped record exists and every candidate status is CANDIDATE. Two limitations are recorded (no independent hash recomputation and no direct access to the 264-event log); neither contradicts any claim checked. This report is information-only evidence for Stage 1 and authorizes nothing.\"\n}\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
